  "raw_label": "postponed_or_procedural",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Kathiravan vs / on 27 March, 2024 Author: Sathi Kumar Sukumara Kurup Bench: Sathi Kumar Sukumara Kurup WP(MD)No.7833 of 2 Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated : 27.03.2024 Coram: The Hon'Ble Mr.Justice Sathi Kumar Sukumara Kurup W.P.(MD)No.7833 of 2024 Kathiravan ... Petitioner /vs./ 1.The Commissioner Madurai City. 2.The Assistant Commissioner Thirupparangundram Division, Madurai City. 3.The Inspector of Police Thirunagar Police Station, Madurai City. 4. The Food Safety Officer, Thirupparankundram Division, Madurai City. 5. The Executive Engineer, Construction and Maintenance Division, (Thallakulam P.W.D. Campus), Madurai -2. ... Respondents (R-4 & 5 are suo-moto impleaded vide order dated 27.03.2024 in W.P.(MD).No.7833 of 2024) ... Respondents 1/6 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis WP(MD)No.7833 PRAYER: Writ Petition filed under Article 226 of the Constitution of India for issuance of Writ of Mandamus, directing the second Respondent to grant permission to conduct Annadhanam and to arrange Spinning Wheel (Rattinam) gaming activities in the Arulmighu Muthurmariamman Temple festival held on 25.03.2024 to 01.04.2024. Kathiravan vs / on 27 March, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/24765846/ 1 For Petitioner : Mr.T.Palanisamy For R1 to 5 : Mr.B.Thanga Aravindh Government Advocate (Criminal Sid ORDER",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "The learned Counsel for the Petitioner submitted thatthe Petitioner had filed this petition, seeking a Writ of Mandamus, directing the second Respondent to grant permission to conduct Annadhanam and to arrange Spinning Wheel (Rattinam) gaming activities in the Arulmighu Muthurmariamman Temple festival held from 25.03.2024 to 01.04.2024. 2. The learned Government Advocate (Criminal Side) appearing for the Respondent Police submits that permission to offer Annadhanam was rejected as the Petitioner had not obtained prior permission from the Food Safety Department and also regarding festival arrangements from the Public Works Department, etc. Therefore, the https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis learned Government Advocate (Criminal Side) further submits that the Petitioner may be directed to submit fresh representation as getting permission from the Food Safety Department is very necessary, considering the fact that the Annadhanam involved several number of people, safety of the common villagers has to be considered. 3. On consideration of the rival submissions, the Petitioner is directed to get prior permission from the Food Safety Officer concerned after filing proper application before the Food Safety Officer."
  },
